# Scene 1, the cold open: a type system can only encode so much. A well-typed Order, and three questions its type
# can't answer.
Import //reels/entities.reelpreset
Screen code

Output //.artifacts/reel/scenes/01-types.mp4
Set Viewport 1600x900
Set FontSize 19

Code //examples/Nullean.Entities.Quickstart/Order.cs
Focus lines 8-25
Say "A type system can only encode so much."
Say@over "This order compiles. But can its total [total] ever go negative?"
Wait [total]
Mark "decimal Total" 1
Callout "decimal Total" "never negative?"
Say@over "Is cancelling it twice [cancel] the same as cancelling once?"
Wait [cancel]
Mark "public Order Cancel()" 2
Callout "public Order Cancel()" "twice the same as once?"
Say@over "Does its version [version] only ever go up?"
Wait [version]
Mark "int Version" 3
Callout "int Version" "only ever goes up?"
Sleep 800ms
Callout off
Say "Types say what your data is. Not what must stay true."
Say@skeptic "So I check it in the constructor. Like everyone does."
Mark off
Focus off
Sleep 300ms
